    "old": "<img alt=\"Five aldehydes: (a) benzaldehyde, a benzene ring with a CHO group; (b) cinnamaldehyde, a benzene ring attached to CH=CH-CHO; (c) vanillin, a benzene ring bearing CHO, OH and OCH3 groups; (d) a C=C double bond with CH3CH2 on one carbon and CH2CHO on the other, both H on the same side (cis-3-hexenal); (e) a nine-carbon chain with two C=C double bonds, CH3CH2-CH=CH-CH2-CH2-CH=CH-CHO (2,6-nonadienal).\" style=\"width: 436px; height: 380px;\" class=\"internal\" src=\"/@api/deki/files/27163/14.6.jpg\" fileid=\"27163\" width=\"436px\" height=\"380px\" />",
    "new": "<img class=\"internal\" alt=\"Five aldehydes, as skeletal structures: (a) benzaldehyde, a benzene ring with a CHO group; (b) cinnamaldehyde, a benzene ring attached to CH=CH-CHO with the chain trans; (c) vanillin, a benzene ring with CHO, an OH across the ring from the CHO, and an OCH3 next to the OH; (d) cis-3-hexenal, a six-carbon chain with CHO at one end and a cis C=C between carbons 3 and 4; (e) trans-2-cis-6-nonadienal, a nine-carbon chain with CHO at one end, a trans C=C at carbons 2-3 and a cis C=C at carbons 6-7.\" width=\"532\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" src=\"/@api/deki/files/{{alds}}/fig-p597103-aldehydes.svg\" fileid=\"{{alds}}\" />",
